model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Request reliability reads Home rows only through the pool time index from the window start, ranks those attempts to find each request's latest one, and looks up by request identity only a request that finished in the window with every Home attempt before it. No predicate ORs the time and identity sets, because that shape scans the pool's whole history. Terminal evidence joins a latest attempt by its start key, and only a canonical UUID request identity can match. Terminal-only rows dedupe against those same attempts. Each terminal table is read at most once per statement part, never once per request partition. Counts, attribution and boundaries are unchanged."
      constraint "The availability check-in still runs every minute. Its request reliability figure is computed with each five-minute history capture, its windows ending at that capture, and the check-in reuses it while it is under six minutes old. A missing, failed or older figure is computed by the check-in and kept for the next ones, so a stopped capture still reaches capture_stale. Breach, failing-now and collection-unavailable signals keep their rules; real-time terminal and gateway evidence reaches them at the next capture instead of the next minute."
    }
  }
}
